%% A manpower request approved in OA, through to the new employee's first day (areas 1 and 2).
%% Receiving the approval is built (area 1); the workflow is area 2's design, and the draft record
%% and its activation are stories B-6 and C-3.
sequenceDiagram
  participant OA as OA (mock)
  participant WH as Area 1: OA webhook
  participant WF as Area 2: workflow
  actor HR as HR, Singapore
  participant M as Area 1: employee master
  actor OPS as Admin operations
  participant N as Teams and DingTalk (mock)

  OA->>WH: approval.completed, HMAC-signed
  WH->>WH: verify the signature and timestamp, then store it once by event id
  WH-->>OA: 202 Accepted (a repeated delivery is ignored)
  WH->>WF: oa.approval.completed (MANPOWER_REQUEST, APPROVED)
  WF->>WF: start once per OA event id: the instance and the recruitment requisition, audited
  HR->>WF: complete the requisition: the hire is confirmed
  WF->>M: create a draft record (PRE_HIRE), linked to the request
  WF->>OPS: laptop, desk and account tasks, each with a due date
  WF->>N: reminders, then escalations once a task passes its SLA
  OPS->>WF: complete the preparation tasks
  WF-->>M: onboarding milestones met
  Note over M: a later SG HR sync brings the verified record
  M->>M: both conditions met: the record becomes active
